Table full name: bigquery-public-data.utility_us.us_states_area
Column name: region_code Type: STRING Description: Current region code. Regions consist of 2 or more divisions
Column name: division_code Type: STRING Description: Current division code. Divisions consist of 2 or more states
Column name: state_fips_code Type: STRING Description: Two digit FIPS code that uniquely identifies each state. See https://www.census.gov/geo/reference/ansi_statetables.html for more information

State names and their corresponding FIPS codes can be found in BigQuery: bigquery-public-data.census_fips_codes.states_2016
Column name: state_gnis_code Type: STRING Description: Current state GNIS code as maintained by USGS. GNIS is a database that contains name and locative information about more than two million physical and cultural features.
Column name: state_geo_id Type: STRING Description: Unique identifier for each state. Identical to state_fips_code
Column name: state_abbreviation Type: STRING Description: 2 letter abbreviation of state name as determined by the United States Postal Service
Column name: state_name Type: STRING Description: Full text name of state
Column name: legal_area_code Type: STRING Description: Current legal/statistical area description code for state
Column name: feature_class_code Type: STRING Description: MAF/TIGER feature class code. G4000 indicates "State or Equivalent Feature"
Column name: functional_status_code Type: STRING Description: Current functional status code. A full list of possible results can be found: https://www.census.gov/geo/reference/funcstat.html
Column name: area_land_meters Type: INT64 Description: Current land area, in square meters
Column name: area_water_meters Type: INT64 Description: Current water area, in square meters
Column name: internal_point_lat Type: STRING Description: Current latitude of the internal point, which is the point at or closest to the state's geographic center
Column name: internal_point_lon Type: STRING Description: Current longitude of the internal point, which is the point at or closest to the state's geographic center
Column name: state_geom Type: GEOGRAPHY Description: Points of a polygon that encompass the state. Should be used for geographic visualization
